f={'id':'RPF-F065','severity':'medium','title':'Empty or initially refused DDC tape heads do not bind initial state','evidence':[{'path':'code/rust/pfp/src/ddc.rs','lines':[378,398]},{'path':'code/rust/pfp/src/ddc.rs','lines':[412,420]},{'path':'code/rust/pfp/src/ddc.rs','lines':[437,471]}],'status':'source-established','detail':'The head starts as SHA256(genesis_root) and incorporates state only after a successful step. Distinct admitted initial states with zero steps have identical lawful=true receipt_head, and distinct first-step refusals also preserve that head. Bind initial state and full request separately, or clearly document head as accepted-prefix-only identity rather than complete request custody.','limits':'No collision in SHA256 asserted. Dispatcher may independently bind an outer request in some call paths; the public verify_tape result itself does not.'}
